non temporal stores ...

my current understanding is that they are very useful for avoiding cache pollution and
the read_to_own on the cacheline


normal stores on writeback memory would take E on the cacheline and then make the writes.
non temporal stores do a write invalidate on the cacheline and the write does not allocate
a cacheline instead goes directly (I hope to llc or dram)


important thing being they are cache coherent by virtue of making sure that cacheline is 
invalidated all across

